From: VyOS LS1046A <build@vyos.io>
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: skip RX PCD scheme creation for all ports

fsl_dpa's dpaa_eth_init_ports() calls dpaa_eth_init_rx_port() which
creates FMan PCD schemes (RSS). When dpa_app later invokes fmc_execute()
to push CDX offload schemes, FM_PCD_KgSchemeSet() fails with "Resource
Already Exists — Scheme id (0)" because the kernel already owns those
scheme IDs.

Fix: make dpaa_eth_init_rx_port() a no-op — return immediately without
creating RX default FQs or PCD schemes. The TX path (dpaa_eth_init_tx_port)
continues to work normally, so the kernel can still transmit frames
(e.g., SSH responses on the management interface).

Tradeoff: kernel cannot receive frames until dpa_app successfully programs
the CDX PCD (~T+64s). Serial console remains available for emergency access.
After dpa_app starts, all RX is handled by CDX FQs.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
@@ -10630,0 +10631,7 @@
 static void
 dpaa_eth_init_rx_port(struct fm_port *port, struct dpa_bp *bp, size_t count,
 		struct dpa_fq *errq, struct dpa_fq *defq,
 		struct dpa_buffer_layout_s *buf_layout)
 {
+	/* Skip RX PCD scheme creation — CDX dataplane (dpa_app → CDX
+	 * kernel module) programs all FMan PCD from scratch. No kernel RSS.
+	 * TX path (dpaa_eth_init_tx_port) is kept for kernel TX (SSH). */
+	return;
+
 	struct fm_port_params rx_port_param;
 	int i;
 	bool frag_enabled = false;
